WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.135
-You know our next guest

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.603
from his Emmy winning
role on "Watchmen."

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:06.639
Now you can see him staring
in the new movie "Candyman" --

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.642
Ooh, it's scary -- which is
in theaters this Friday.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:14.213
Please welcome
Yahya Abdul-Mateen II.

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:17.216
That's my man! Yo!

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:19.251
Welcome!
-Oh, keep it going.

00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:20.954
-You want more? You want more?
-Keep it going.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:21.987
You want more?
-Yeah, let me --

00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:24.758
-Yeah, come on.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:27.226
I can't see you
from the waist down.

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:33.065 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:38.938 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:42.041
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:44.010
-Yeah, man. You can't
cheat me out the music.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.446
You can't cheat me
out the music, man, you know?

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.147
I need that.
-I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:49.949
Thank you for doing our show.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.284
Man, you're blowing up, bud.

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.353
It's all happening.

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:56.088
You were on the cover
of the "Hollywood Reporter"

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:57.990
saying that
you're the new A list.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.960
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.529
It's cool. That's cool.

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:03.963
-Is there ever a part of it

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.398
where it's like
a pinch-me moment

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.700
where you go, "Yeah, I can't
believe this is my life"?

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.170
-Yeah, man. You know,
every once in a while,

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.272
you know, you end up
in these certain scenarios.

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:16.575
You know, I try to basically
live as normal life as possible

00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:18.644
and things like that.
And I do, for the most part.

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:22.548
But then, you know, sometimes,
you end up in situations.

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.650
Once I was at a party --

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:27.353
At a Oscars party, right?
Go figure.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:31.991
And, you know, Jay-Z throws
this party, the Gold Party,

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.859
and he throws it every year
for the Oscars.

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:35.928
I got an invitation,
and I'm in there.

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:37.196
You know, I'm in my tux,

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:39.532
and I'm dressed up,
feeling good.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.100
And one of my favorite songs
comes on.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.935
It's like a Juvenile song.

00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:46.539
I hop on the stage, and
I'm dancing, and I'm sweating.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.674
And I'm just, like --
I forget where I am.

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:52.578
I just lose all my,
you know, scruples.

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:55.948
And I look over, and Jay-Z's
looking me dead in my eyes.

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:57.817
You know, no judgment
or nothing like that.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:01.854
But he's looking at me, and
I saw myself through his eyes.

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:03.890
Was like, "Yeah, I should
probably hop down off the stage.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.791
I should probably
get off the stage right now.

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:07.627
You know, play it cool.
Play it cool."

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.094
-Yeah, exactly, right, yeah.

00:02:09.094 --> 00:02:10.763
-But it's cool to get
carried away, you know?

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:14.600
-Yeah. You're the youngest of
six siblings, is that correct?

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.135
-Yeah, yeah, yeah,
youngest of six.

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:19.072
-Do they keep you grounded?

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.040
-Not the girls, but my brother
does.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.708
My brother does for sure.
Like, the girls --

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:26.712
They just, you know, they give
me wings, and they support me.

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:29.148
My brother supports me,
but he kind of does this thing

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:32.818
where he -- It's like
he gives me the tough love,

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:35.053
like a heavy, heavy, heavy dose
of the tough love,

00:02:35.053 --> 00:02:36.455
you know what I'm saying?

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:39.258
Like, I post a picture
that I've been working out.

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:41.527
I'm trying to gain weight and
get my muscles for "Aquaman,"

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:43.495
and he'll be the one
in the comment

00:02:43.495 --> 00:02:45.197
talking about skipping leg day.

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:46.933
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.835
-Yeah, yeah, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.370
-I try to get
back in shape, right?

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.339
I'm posting a video
of me dunking a basketball.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.140
And he's like, "Yeah,
I saw you posted the video

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.176
getting 2 inches
off the ground."

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:58.444
And I'm like, "Yeah, okay, man.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.312
I was actually
proud about that."

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:01.581
-He's a good man.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.916
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. But you
need that. You need that.

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:05.885
-I want to talk
about "Candyman."

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:09.288
-Oh, yeah.
-I remember the original.

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:11.457
This is -- It's not a remake.

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.859
This is a continuation
of the story.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:16.829
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. No, it's not
a remake. It's a continuation.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:20.466
Our "Candyman" picks up about 30
years after the original story.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.769
It's set in present-day Chicago,

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:25.971
and, you know, I think it's
a refreshing take on Candyman.

00:03:25.971 --> 00:03:28.440
You know, by going back to
Chicago 30 years after,

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:31.077
it gives us a chance
to, you know,

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:34.046
to talk about some of the social
issues that affect Chicago

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:36.082
and Cabrini Green today

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.150
while also, at the same time,
giving the fans,

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.619
you know, the loyal fans,

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.854
some of the things that they
know and love about "Candyman,"

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:44.089
you know, the frightening
moments,

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:46.693
the horror elements

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.394
that people have come to know
for a long time.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:51.897
But we get to put our own
fresh twist on it, also.

00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:54.300
-Did you --
I know it's a movie --

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.837
-Yeah.
-And I know it's a fake story.

00:03:58.837 --> 00:04:01.540
But did you actually
ever say "Candyman"

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.609
five times in a mirror?

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.612
I mean, you did in --
-You said five times?

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.046
-Yeah.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:10.717
-No. No, I don't have
a good reason to do that.

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.718
No, I don't have a good reason
to do that.

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:15.587
Four. I'll give you four.
I'll give you like my best four.

00:04:15.587 --> 00:04:18.591
-Exactly! I can give you four.
Exactly, you're right.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.159
-Exactly, right.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.694
I got a good thing
going on right now.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.830
So I'm trying
to keep it that way.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.533
-I haven't --
There's no mirrors here,

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.135
and I've said it
probably a couple times.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.569
But anyway, it doesn't matter.

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:32.205
We're good. We're cool.

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.672
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.672 --> 00:04:34.707
That's what I say,
like, to ghosts,

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.709
if I think there's ghosts.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.077
I just go,
"Hey, we're cool, right?"

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:40.212
You can do whatever you want.

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:41.614
Ghosts come in through walls.

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.716
-Wait, wait, wait --

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:44.750
-Whatever ghosts want to do.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.285
-Jimmy, you believe in ghosts?

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:48.320
-Sure.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:51.490
-You know what?
It helps to believe in them

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.825
because if you don't
believe in them,

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.126
they might take that personal.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:56.295
So, if any ghosts
in the house right now,

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:57.462
I believe in you.

00:04:57.462 --> 00:04:59.265
I support you dreams.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:03.135
I support your ghost ambitions.
[ Applause ]

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:05.104
-That's exactly right.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:07.206
-You know what I'm sayin'?

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.908
-I want to show a clip.

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:13.045
Here's Yahya Abdul-Mateen II
in "Candyman."

00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:14.446
Take a look at this.

00:05:14.446 --> 00:05:17.683
-The legend is,
if you say his name five times

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:19.786
while looking in the mirror,

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:23.322
he appears in the reflection
and kills you.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:24.490
-Mm.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:28.994
So, I thought that we could --

00:05:28.994 --> 00:05:31.731
-[ Chuckles ]
What did you think?

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.032
-Summon him.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.566
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:34.566 --> 00:05:37.202
Hell no.

00:05:37.202 --> 00:05:38.470
No.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.139
-Candyman.

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:41.406
-Anthony.

00:05:41.406 --> 00:05:44.176
-Candyman.
-Anthony, no.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:45.744
-Candyman.
-Stop.

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:46.979
Stop it.
-Candyman.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.114
-Stop it.

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:49.181
-Okay.

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:50.583
-You better not
do that last one.

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.752
-Okay, okay, okay.

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:54.853 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:54.853 --> 00:05:57.423
[ Whispering ] Candyman.
-See, you playing --

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:58.824
-No, no, stop!

00:05:58.824 --> 00:06:00.092
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:00.092 --> 00:06:02.594
-No!

00:06:02.594 --> 00:06:06.398
Yahya Abdul-Mateen II!

00:06:06.398 --> 00:06:09.035
"Candyman" is in theaters
this Friday!

